{"card":{"card_id":"ma-c-766cd1644d24323fd8d5","statement":"Let $f: H_1\\to H_2$ be a homomorphism of connected algebraic groups.\n\n- If $\\Ch_{\\chi_2}\\in \\mathrm{CS}(H_2)$, then $\\Ch_{\\chi_1}:=f^*\\Ch_{\\chi_2}\\in \\mathrm{CS}(H_1)$. The pullback functor $f^*: \\shv(H_2)\\to \\shv(H_1)$ restricts to a pullback functor $f^*: \\shv_{(\\chi_2\\mbox{-})\\mon}(H_2)\\to\\shv_{(\\chi_1\\mbox{-})\\mon}(H_1)$. The functor $f^*: \\shv_{\\mon}(H_2)\\to \\shv_{\\mon}(H_1)$ admits a (continuous) right adjoint, denoted by $f_*^{\\mon}$. When $f$ is surjective, we have\n\n\\[\nf_*^{\\mon}=f_*|_{\\shv_{\\mon}(H_1)}.\n\\]\n\nIn general, we have\n\n\\[\nf_*^{\\mon}= \\av^{\\mon}\\circ (f_*|_{\\shv_{\\mon}(H_1)}).\n\\]\n\n- When $f$ is surjective, the usual compactly supported pushforward functor $f_!$ restricts to a functor between monodromic categories, which is the left adjoint of $f^!=f^*\\langle \\dim H_2-\\dim H_1\\rangle$. In addition, we have the following isomorphism of functors\n\n\\begin{equation}\nf_![d]\\cong f_*: \\shv_{\\mon}(H_1)\\to \\shv_{\\mon}(H_2),\n\\end{equation}\n\nfor some integer $d$ depending on $\\ker f$.","source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","cluster":"representation_theory","statement_sha256":"8497f28d880f925b393fd89a2c6b6a52a7facec87662f77b62299d26d29ad42d","kind":"proposition","label":"Proposition 238","ref_key":"lem: functoriality depth zero geom Langlands for tori","name":"","order":332,"deps":[],"cite_keys":[],"provenance":{"source_url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.07482","harvest_mode":"arxiv_eprint","payload_sha256":"1b700e8c4a2fc6f0c0f522039f223820ba6737a9a0ac91aea37c58ba7a3389c2","line":7170,"origin":"latex_env","retrieved_at":"2026-09-28T11:10:54+08:00"},"wash":{"version":"cardwash.v2","stages":["segment","purify","classify","dedupe","emit"],"numbering":"document_order_with_label_heuristic","detail":{"stripped_proof":false,"chars":1004,"math_hints":104}}},"paper":{"source_id":"arXiv:2504.07482","title":"Tame categorical local Langlands correspo